  "files": {},
  "metadata": {
    "title": "VLMs connect vision to language; VLAs add action",
    "description": "A VLM maps image patches through a vision encoder and connector into the LLM embedding space alongside text, then produces text or structured answers. A VLA extends the VLM with an action head that emits robot-control tokens in a closed loop. A label-only pipeline loses fine-grained visual information."
  }
}
